# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample-based Krylov Quantum Diagonalization ([SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702)) is a quantum-centric variant of subspace diagonalization. Rather than sampling a single variational ansatz (as in plain sample-based quantum diagonalization ([SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068))) or an ensemble of randomized time-evolution circuits (as in [SqDRIFT](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started)), it samples a *Krylov* basis: the family of states\n"
msgstr "Sample-based Krylov Quantum Diagonalization ([SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702)) adalah varian diagonalisasi subruang yang berpusat pada kuantum. Alih-alih men-sample satu ansatz variasional (seperti pada sample-based quantum diagonalization ([SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068)) biasa) atau ensemble circuit evolusi waktu acak (seperti pada [SqDRIFT](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started)), metode ini men-sample basis *Krylov*: keluarga keadaan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_k \\rangle = e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H} \\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle, \\qquad k = 0, 1, \\dots,\n"
"D - 1,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_k \\rangle = e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H} \\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle, \\qquad k = 0, 1, \\dots,\n"
"D - 1,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "obtained by evolving a reference state $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ for increasing multiples of a fixed time step $\\Delta t$. Bitstrings sampled from these $D$ circuits populate the Krylov subspace in which the Hamiltonian is subsequently diagonalized classically.\n"
msgstr "yang diperoleh dengan mengevolusikan keadaan referensi $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ selama kelipatan yang makin besar dari langkah waktu tetap $\\Delta t$. Bitstring yang di-sample dari $D$ circuit ini mengisi subruang Krylov tempat Hamiltonian kemudian didiagonalisasi secara klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide reproduces the circuit-construction step of the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) algorithm for the single-impurity Anderson model (SIAM), a magnetic impurity coupled to a non-interacting bath, following the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini mereproduksi langkah konstruksi circuit dari algoritma [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) untuk single-impurity Anderson model (SIAM), yaitu sebuah impuritas magnetik yang terhubung ke bath tanpa interaksi, mengikuti publikasi [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The SKQD sampling step works only if the ground state is **sparse** in the computational basis: the classical diagonalization must be able to reconstruct it from a manageable number of sampled bitstrings. As shown below, that sparsity is not automatic; it is a property of the single-particle basis in which the problem is expressed. Getting the basis right is the crux of this construction.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Langkah sampling SKQD hanya bekerja kalau ground state-nya **sparse** di basis komputasional: diagonalisasi klasik harus bisa merekonstruksinya dari sejumlah bitstring hasil sampling yang masih terkelola. Seperti yang ditunjukkan di bawah, sparsity itu tidak otomatis ada; ia adalah properti dari basis partikel tunggal tempat masalahnya dinyatakan. Memilih basis yang tepat adalah kunci dari konstruksi ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Build the SIAM Hamiltonian as a fermionic operator {#1-build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator}"
msgstr "1. Bangun Hamiltonian SIAM sebagai operator fermionik {#1-build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The single-impurity Anderson model places one interacting impurity orbital (index $0$) in contact with a non-interacting bath of $L$ sites arranged as a chain. Its Hamiltonian splits into a one-body part $H_1$ and a two-body part $H_2$,\n"
msgstr "Single-impurity Anderson model menempatkan satu orbital impuritas yang berinteraksi (indeks $0$) bersentuhan dengan bath tanpa interaksi berisi $L$ situs yang tersusun sebagai rantai. Hamiltoniannya terbagi menjadi bagian satu-badan $H_1$ dan bagian dua-badan $H_2$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = H_1 + H_2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = H_1 + H_2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with the one-body part collecting the impurity on-site energy (the chemical potential $\\mu$), the impurity–bath hybridization $V$, and the nearest-neighbor bath hopping $t$,\n"
msgstr "dengan bagian satu-badan mengumpulkan energi on-site impuritas (potensial kimia $\\mu$), hibridisasi impuritas–bath $V$, dan hopping bath tetangga terdekat $t$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_1 = \\mu \\sum_\\sigma a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{0\\sigma}\n"
"      - V \\sum_\\sigma \\left( a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{1\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right)\n"
"      - t \\sum_{\\sigma} \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1}\n"
"        \\left( a^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} a_{i+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_1 = \\mu \\sum_\\sigma a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{0\\sigma}\n"
"      - V \\sum_\\sigma \\left( a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{1\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right)\n"
"      - t \\sum_{\\sigma} \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1}\n"
"        \\left( a^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} a_{i+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the two-body part carrying the on-site Coulomb repulsion $U$ on the impurity alone,\n"
msgstr "dan bagian dua-badan membawa tolakan Coulomb on-site $U$ pada impuritas saja,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_2 = U \\, a^\\dagger_{0\\uparrow} a_{0\\uparrow} a^\\dagger_{0\\downarrow} a_{0\\downarrow}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_2 = U \\, a^\\dagger_{0\\uparrow} a_{0\\uparrow} a^\\dagger_{0\\downarrow} a_{0\\downarrow}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide works at the particle-hole-symmetric point $\\mu = -U/2$. These two parts map directly onto the one-body integrals `h1e` (bath hopping, impurity hybridization, impurity on-site energy) and the single two-body integral `h2e` (the impurity Coulomb term). First assemble them in the position basis, where the model is naturally defined.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini bekerja di titik simetris partikel-lubang $\\mu = -U/2$. Kedua bagian ini terpetakan langsung ke integral satu-badan `h1e` (hopping bath, hibridisasi impuritas, energi on-site impuritas) dan satu integral dua-badan `h2e` (suku Coulomb impuritas). Rakit keduanya dulu di basis posisi, tempat model ini secara alami didefinisikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"change-to-the-momentum-basis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Change to the momentum basis {#2-change-to-the-momentum-basis}"
msgstr "2. Pindah ke basis momentum {#2-change-to-the-momentum-basis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bath part of the SIAM is a free-fermion chain, so it is diagonalized by a change to the momentum basis. This is the decisive step for SKQD. Because the bath is translationally invariant, the ground state is not sparse in the position basis, but it is sparse in the momentum basis, where the bath Hamiltonian is diagonal. The single-particle orbital rotation that performs this change is problem-specific linear algebra. It diagonalizes the bath hopping matrix while leaving the impurity orbital untouched, then relocates the impurity to a central site:\n"
msgstr "Bagian bath dari SIAM adalah rantai fermion bebas, jadi ia didiagonalisasi dengan pindah ke basis momentum. Ini langkah penentu untuk SKQD. Karena bath-nya invarian terhadap translasi, ground state tidak sparse di basis posisi, tapi sparse di basis momentum, tempat Hamiltonian bath-nya diagonal. Rotasi orbital partikel tunggal yang melakukan perpindahan ini adalah aljabar linear khusus masalah. Rotasi ini mendiagonalisasi matriks hopping bath sambil membiarkan orbital impuritas tidak tersentuh, lalu memindahkan impuritas ke situs tengah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike a variational workflow, this rotates the Hamiltonian integrals into the momentum basis, so that the whole circuit (Hamiltonian and state alike) lives in the basis where the ground state is sparse and the sampled bitstrings are therefore informative. Rotating the one- and two-body integrals is a standard basis change of the electronic-structure tensors:\n"
msgstr "Berbeda dengan workflow variasional, di sini integral Hamiltonian-lah yang dirotasi ke basis momentum, sehingga seluruh circuit (baik Hamiltonian maupun keadaannya) berada di basis tempat ground state sparse dan bitstring hasil sampling karena itu informatif. Merotasi integral satu- dan dua-badan adalah perubahan basis standar untuk tensor struktur elektronik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the rotation leaves the impurity orbital fixed (it acts only on the bath), the on-site interaction is unchanged. `h2e_momentum` remains a single number-number term, just like `h2e`. The only change is that the impurity has been relocated to a central index. This is visible directly in the integral tensors, which each carry one nonzero entry:\n"
msgstr "Karena rotasi membiarkan orbital impuritas tetap (ia hanya bekerja pada bath), interaksi on-site tidak berubah. `h2e_momentum` tetap berupa satu suku number-number, persis seperti `h2e`. Satu-satunya perubahan adalah impuritas dipindahkan ke indeks tengah. Ini terlihat langsung di tensor integralnya, yang masing-masing membawa satu entri tak nol:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This locality is what keeps the interaction cheap to synthesize later.\n"
msgstr "Lokalitas inilah yang membuat interaksi tetap murah untuk disintesis nanti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble the one-body integrals into a [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") with the electronic-integral constructor [`from_1body_tril_spin_sym()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym\"), which expects them packed into lower-triangular ordering. The two-body part is a single number-number term, so rather than routing it through the two-body integral machinery, build it directly with [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-cre#qiskit_fermions.operators.cre \"qiskit_fermions.operators.cre\")/[`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-ann#qiskit_fermions.operators.ann \"qiskit_fermions.operators.ann\"): the on-site Coulomb operator $U \\, n_{p\\uparrow} n_{p\\downarrow}$ for the impurity mode $p$ (its $\\uparrow$ mode at index `p`, its $\\downarrow$ mode at index `p + norb` in the block-spin layout). Both constructors spin-double the `norb` spatial orbitals into `2 * norb` fermionic modes.\n"
msgstr "Rakit integral satu-badan menjadi sebuah [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") dengan konstruktor integral elektronik [`from_1body_tril_spin_sym()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym\"), yang mengharapkan integral dikemas dalam urutan segitiga bawah. Bagian dua-badan adalah satu suku number-number, jadi daripada melewatkannya lewat mesin integral dua-badan, bangun langsung dengan [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-cre#qiskit_fermions.operators.cre \"qiskit_fermions.operators.cre\")/[`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-ann#qiskit_fermions.operators.ann \"qiskit_fermions.operators.ann\"): operator Coulomb on-site $U \\, n_{p\\uparrow} n_{p\\downarrow}$ untuk mode impuritas $p$ (mode $\\uparrow$-nya di indeks `p`, mode $\\downarrow$-nya di indeks `p + norb` pada tata letak block-spin). Kedua konstruktor menggandakan spin `norb` orbital spasial menjadi `2 * norb` mode fermionik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the one-body part $H_1$ and the two-body part $H_2$ as separate operators rather than summing them eagerly, matching the terms $H_1$ and $H_2$ of the section-1 equations. Building each piece once (in both bases) makes them reusable below. Summed, they give the full Hamiltonian for the exact diagonalization in either basis. Individually, $H_2$ (momentum basis) is the operator the Trotter step evolves in step 4.\n"
msgstr "Pertahankan bagian satu-badan $H_1$ dan bagian dua-badan $H_2$ sebagai operator terpisah, jangan langsung dijumlahkan, sesuai dengan suku $H_1$ dan $H_2$ pada persamaan di bagian 1. Membangun tiap bagian sekali saja (di kedua basis) membuatnya bisa dipakai ulang di bawah. Kalau dijumlahkan, keduanya membentuk Hamiltonian penuh untuk diagonalisasi eksak di basis mana pun. Secara terpisah, $H_2$ (basis momentum) adalah operator yang dievolusikan oleh langkah Trotter di langkah 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The basis change is a unitary similarity transform, so it leaves the spectrum untouched. Confirm the operator is correct by comparing its lowest eigenvalue in the $(\\text{norb}, \\text{nelec})$ sector against an exact diagonalization. The [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") exposes a SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") (backed by a native full configuration interaction (FCI) matrix-vector kernel), so it can be handed straight to [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\").\n"
msgstr "Perubahan basis adalah transformasi kesamaan uniter, jadi spektrumnya tidak berubah. Pastikan operatornya benar dengan membandingkan eigenvalue terendahnya di sektor $(\\text{norb}, \\text{nelec})$ terhadap diagonalisasi eksak. [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") menyediakan SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") (didukung kernel perkalian matriks-vektor full configuration interaction (FCI) native), sehingga bisa langsung diberikan ke [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff of the basis change is sparsity. To make it concrete, count how many computational-basis determinants are needed to capture 99% of the ground-state weight, and compare the momentum basis against the position basis. The energy is basis-independent, but the number of determinants is not:\n"
msgstr "Keuntungan dari perubahan basis adalah sparsity. Biar konkret, hitung berapa banyak determinan basis komputasional yang dibutuhkan untuk menangkap 99% bobot ground state, lalu bandingkan basis momentum dengan basis posisi. Energinya tidak bergantung pada basis, tapi jumlah determinannya tidak demikian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two operators share the same energy, but the position-basis ground state is spread over thousands of determinants, while the momentum basis concentrates it onto around 20, which is why SKQD sampling works in the momentum basis and not the position basis.\n"
msgstr "Kedua operator punya energi yang sama, tapi ground state di basis posisi tersebar di ribuan determinan, sedangkan basis momentum memusatkannya ke sekitar 20, makanya sampling SKQD bekerja di basis momentum dan bukan di basis posisi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"prepare-the-reference-state\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Prepare the reference state {#3-prepare-the-reference-state}"
msgstr "3. Siapkan keadaan referensi {#3-prepare-the-reference-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SKQD reference $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ is the superposition of all excitations of the electrons closest to the Fermi level into the nearest empty momentum modes. The [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication builds it with a hand-written network of [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)s. It looks strongly correlated (it has hundreds of nonzero computational-basis amplitudes), but a network of number-conserving two-mode rotations is a single-particle (fermionic Gaussian) operation, so the state it produces is a single Slater determinant. That means you can prepare it with one [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate, given the single-particle rotation the network implements.\n"
msgstr "Referensi SKQD $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ adalah superposisi dari semua eksitasi elektron yang paling dekat dengan level Fermi ke mode momentum kosong terdekat. Publikasi [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) membangunnya dengan jaringan [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) yang ditulis manual. Keadaan ini tampak berkorelasi kuat (punya ratusan amplitudo basis komputasional tak nol), tapi jaringan rotasi dua-mode yang menjaga jumlah partikel adalah operasi partikel tunggal (Gaussian fermionik), sehingga keadaan yang dihasilkannya adalah satu determinan Slater. Artinya, kamu bisa menyiapkannya dengan satu gate [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\"), asalkan rotasi partikel tunggal yang diimplementasikan jaringan itu diketahui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because each [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) acts as a Givens rotation on a pair of modes, that rotation can be built directly in the single-particle picture (one Givens matrix per gate) instead of emitting the two-qubit gates by hand. The gates form a brickwork of nearest-neighbor rotations that fans out from the Fermi level in expanding layers, spreading each near-Fermi electron across the empty modes just above it:\n"
msgstr "Karena setiap [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) bekerja sebagai rotasi Givens pada sepasang mode, rotasi itu bisa dibangun langsung di gambaran partikel tunggal (satu matriks Givens per gate) daripada mengeluarkan gate dua-qubit secara manual. Gate-gate itu membentuk brickwork rotasi tetangga terdekat yang menyebar dari level Fermi dalam lapisan-lapisan yang meluas, menyebarkan tiap elektron dekat-Fermi ke mode kosong tepat di atasnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The rotation above is expressed in the momentum basis, matching the Hamiltonian. The electrons near the Fermi level are the highest-energy occupied momentum modes, and the network excites them into the lowest-energy empty ones. This is why the reference must be built after the basis change of the previous step, not before.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Rotasi di atas dinyatakan di basis momentum, sesuai dengan Hamiltonian. Elektron di dekat level Fermi adalah mode momentum terisi berenergi tertinggi, dan jaringan itu mengeksitasi mereka ke mode kosong berenergi terendah. Inilah sebabnya referensi harus dibangun setelah perubahan basis di langkah sebelumnya, bukan sebelumnya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Slater determinant preparation is done per spin sector, since each sector has its own (electrons, orbitals) shape. A single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate (an occupation, the lowest `nocc` modes filled, together with the single-particle rotation) prepares one sector; the same gate is applied once on the alpha modes `0..norb` and once on the beta modes `norb..2*norb`, since both spin sectors share the same reference occupation and rotation here:\n"
msgstr "Persiapan determinan Slater dilakukan per sektor spin, karena tiap sektor punya bentuk (elektron, orbital) sendiri. Satu gate [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") (sebuah okupansi, yaitu `nocc` mode terendah terisi, bersama rotasi partikel tunggal) menyiapkan satu sektor; gate yang sama diterapkan sekali pada mode alpha `0..norb` dan sekali pada mode beta `norb..2*norb`, karena kedua sektor spin di sini berbagi okupansi referensi dan rotasi yang sama:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This declarative gate replaces the hand-coded [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) network; the transpiler generates the Givens-rotation synthesis.\n"
msgstr "Gate deklaratif ini menggantikan jaringan [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) yang di-coding manual; transpiler yang menghasilkan sintesis rotasi Givens.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"assemble-the-krylov-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Assemble the Krylov circuits {#4-assemble-the-krylov-circuits}"
msgstr "4. Rakit circuit Krylov {#4-assemble-the-krylov-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each Krylov circuit is the reference-state preparation followed by evolution under $e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H}$. Split the Hamiltonian into its one-body and two-body parts, $H = H_1 + H_2$, and Trotterize the evolution over that split. This is the decisive choice for circuit depth. The one-body evolution $e^{-i t H_1}$ is a free-fermion (fermionic Gaussian) operation, so it is a single-particle basis rotation (an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") with unitary $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$) rather than something that has to be Pauli-Trotterized term by term. The two-body evolution $e^{-i t H_2}$ acts only on the single on-site interaction term. Building the step this way lets the transpiler emit a shallow brickwork of Givens rotations plus a single two-qubit interaction gate, the shallow structure that the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication builds by hand.\n"
msgstr "Setiap circuit Krylov adalah persiapan keadaan referensi diikuti evolusi di bawah $e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H}$. Pisahkan Hamiltonian menjadi bagian satu-badan dan dua-badan, $H = H_1 + H_2$, lalu lakukan Trotterisasi evolusi atas pemisahan itu. Ini pilihan penentu untuk kedalaman circuit. Evolusi satu-badan $e^{-i t H_1}$ adalah operasi fermion bebas (Gaussian fermionik), jadi ia berupa rotasi basis partikel tunggal (sebuah [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") dengan uniter $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$) dan bukan sesuatu yang harus di-Trotterisasi Pauli suku demi suku. Evolusi dua-badan $e^{-i t H_2}$ hanya bekerja pada satu suku interaksi on-site. Dengan membangun langkah seperti ini, transpiler bisa menghasilkan brickwork rotasi Givens yang dangkal plus satu gate interaksi dua-qubit, struktur dangkal yang dibangun secara manual oleh publikasi [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We already have the two-body part. It is the `two_body_momentum` operator built in step 2 (the single on-site term). The one-body evolution $e^{-i t H_1}$ is spin-independent, so it is a single per-sector [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") with unitary $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$ applied once to each spin sector, the same parallel structure as the reference-state preparation.\n"
msgstr "Kita sudah punya bagian dua-badan. Itu adalah operator `two_body_momentum` yang dibangun di langkah 2 (satu suku on-site). Evolusi satu-badan $e^{-i t H_1}$ tidak bergantung pada spin, jadi ia berupa satu [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") per sektor dengan uniter $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$ yang diterapkan sekali ke tiap sektor spin, dengan struktur paralel yang sama seperti persiapan keadaan referensi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each Krylov circuit evolves for a total time $k \\, \\Delta t$. That is realized with a second-order Trotter product of $k$ steps of size $\\Delta t$, so the per-step error stays fixed as the Krylov dimension grows. Each step sandwiches a full one-body rotation (one per spin sector) between two half-steps of the (cheap, single-term) two-body evolution. The Krylov dimension $D$ is the number of such circuits, with `dim` ranging from `0` (reference state only) to $D - 1$.\n"
msgstr "Setiap circuit Krylov berevolusi selama total waktu $k \\, \\Delta t$. Itu diwujudkan dengan produk Trotter orde kedua dari $k$ langkah berukuran $\\Delta t$, sehingga galat per langkah tetap konstan seiring bertambahnya dimensi Krylov. Setiap langkah mengapit satu rotasi satu-badan penuh (satu per sektor spin) di antara dua setengah-langkah evolusi dua-badan (yang murah, satu suku). Dimensi Krylov $D$ adalah jumlah circuit semacam itu, dengan `dim` berkisar dari `0` (hanya keadaan referensi) sampai $D - 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The circuits built here carry no measurements yet, because the same fermionic circuits also drive the exact simulation in step 6, and a measurement is not a unitary operation. Step 5 adds them with [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\"), which reads mode `i` into classical bit `i`.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Circuit yang dibangun di sini belum membawa pengukuran, karena circuit fermionik yang sama juga dipakai untuk simulasi eksak di langkah 6, dan pengukuran bukan operasi uniter. Langkah 5 menambahkannya dengan [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\"), yang membaca mode `i` ke bit klasik `i`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Prefer measuring the *fermionic* circuit over the transpiled one. A fermionic measurement names the mode it reads, so layout and routing carry it along with the qubit that mode ended up on, and the sampled bitstring is indexed by mode. Measuring the transpiled circuit instead leaves you to undo [`final_index_layout()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.TranspileLayout#final_index_layout) yourself, and silently returns permuted results if you forget. This relies on the occupation-basis Jordan-Wigner encoding the preset uses, where each mode is carried by one qubit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Lebih baik mengukur circuit *fermionik* daripada circuit hasil transpile. Pengukuran fermionik menyebut mode yang dibacanya, sehingga layout dan routing membawanya bersama qubit tempat mode itu berakhir, dan bitstring hasil sampling diindeks berdasarkan mode. Kalau kamu mengukur circuit hasil transpile, kamu harus membatalkan [`final_index_layout()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.TranspileLayout#final_index_layout) sendiri, dan hasilnya diam-diam akan tertukar kalau kamu lupa. Ini mengandalkan encoding Jordan-Wigner basis okupansi yang dipakai preset, di mana tiap mode dibawa oleh satu qubit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-to-qubit-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Transpile to qubit circuits {#5-transpile-to-qubit-circuits}"
msgstr "5. Transpile ke circuit qubit {#5-transpile-to-qubit-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiling a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") maps its fermionic gates to qubit gates. This uses the Jordan-Wigner [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") mapping. The [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates synthesize into a brickwork of Givens rotations, and the single-term [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") lowers to a single two-qubit interaction gate.\n"
msgstr "Men-transpile sebuah [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") memetakan gate fermioniknya ke gate qubit. Ini memakai pemetaan Jordan-Wigner [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\"). Gate [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") disintesis menjadi brickwork rotasi Givens, dan [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") satu suku diturunkan menjadi satu gate interaksi dua-qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because every fermionic gate here has a default synthesis, you can use the ready-made [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") directly rather than hand-assembling the stages. Any keyword arguments are forwarded to the qubit stage; pass `optimization_level=0` for a faithful, unoptimized picture of the synthesized depth. Generating the full family of Krylov circuits is then a loop over the Krylov dimension. Keep the untranspiled [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")s alongside the transpiled qubit circuits. The fermionic ones drive the exact (statevector) simulation in step 6, so they must stay measurement-free; `measure_all(inplace=False)` returns a measured copy to transpile and leaves the original untouched, and that copy is what a backend would execute.\n"
msgstr "Karena setiap gate fermionik di sini punya sintesis default, kamu bisa langsung memakai [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") yang sudah jadi daripada merakit tahapannya sendiri. Keyword argument apa pun diteruskan ke tahap qubit; berikan `optimization_level=0` untuk gambaran kedalaman hasil sintesis yang apa adanya dan tanpa optimasi. Menghasilkan seluruh keluarga circuit Krylov tinggal berupa loop atas dimensi Krylov. Simpan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") yang belum di-transpile berdampingan dengan circuit qubit hasil transpile. Yang fermionik menjalankan simulasi eksak (statevector) di langkah 6, jadi harus tetap bebas pengukuran; `measure_all(inplace=False)` mengembalikan salinan berpengukuran untuk di-transpile dan membiarkan aslinya tidak tersentuh, dan salinan itulah yang akan dieksekusi backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Krylov dimension shows up directly in the circuits’ two-qubit depth. The reference-state preparation is a fixed cost, and each additional Krylov power adds another second-order Trotter step of the time-evolution operator.\n"
msgstr "Dimensi Krylov terlihat langsung pada kedalaman dua-qubit circuit. Persiapan keadaan referensi adalah biaya tetap, dan setiap pangkat Krylov tambahan menambah satu langkah Trotter orde kedua lagi dari operator evolusi waktu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Splitting the Hamiltonian keeps these depths modest. The one-body evolution is a genuine orbital rotation, so it synthesizes to an [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) brickwork on adjacent qubits. Each half step of the on-site interaction is a single [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate) coupling the impurity’s two spin modes; the cheap term that the second-order product sandwiches around the rotation. Handing the whole Hamiltonian to one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate instead would Pauli-Trotterize the one-body part term by term, propagating long Jordan-Wigner `Z`-strings across the (long-range) impurity-bath couplings and inflating the depth by an order of magnitude.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Memisahkan Hamiltonian menjaga kedalaman ini tetap sedang. Evolusi satu-badan adalah rotasi orbital sejati, jadi ia disintesis menjadi brickwork [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) pada qubit yang bersebelahan. Setiap setengah-langkah interaksi on-site adalah satu [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate) yang menghubungkan dua mode spin impuritas; suku murah yang diapit produk orde kedua di sekitar rotasi. Kalau seluruh Hamiltonian diberikan ke satu gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\"), bagian satu-badan akan di-Trotterisasi Pauli suku demi suku, merambatkan `Z`-string Jordan-Wigner yang panjang melintasi kopling impuritas-bath (jarak jauh) dan menggelembungkan kedalaman hingga satu orde magnitudo.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first circuit prepares only the reference determinant, while the last carries the most Trotter steps (four in this case):\n"
msgstr "Circuit pertama hanya menyiapkan determinan referensi, sedangkan yang terakhir membawa langkah Trotter terbanyak (empat dalam kasus ini):\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The reference-state preparation circuit (Krylov dimension 0).](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-13.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The reference-state preparation circuit (Krylov dimension 0).](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-13.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A second-order Trotter Krylov circuit with four evolution steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-14.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A second-order Trotter Krylov circuit with four evolution steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-14.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Sample bitstrings from the Krylov circuits {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"
msgstr "6. Sample bitstring dari circuit Krylov {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, you would run the transpiled circuits and measure. This is the noiseless (statevector) version of that step, showing the bitstrings SKQD would collect. Simulate each untranspiled [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") with [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") and sample the resulting statevector with [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"
msgstr "Di hardware, kamu akan menjalankan circuit hasil transpile lalu mengukurnya. Ini adalah versi tanpa noise (statevector) dari langkah itu, yang menunjukkan bitstring yang akan dikumpulkan SKQD. Simulasikan tiap [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") yang belum di-transpile dengan [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") lalu sample statevector hasilnya dengan [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate is validate-then-rotate under simulation (it checks that the incoming state occupies its reference determinant, then applies the rotation). Therefore, the input is the plain occupation determinant: the lowest `nocc` modes filled per spin, with no rotation. The gate applies `reference_rotation` itself.\n"
msgstr "Gate [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") bersifat validasi-lalu-rotasi saat simulasi (ia memeriksa bahwa keadaan masukan menempati determinan referensinya, lalu menerapkan rotasi). Karena itu, inputnya adalah determinan okupansi biasa: `nocc` mode terendah terisi per spin, tanpa rotasi. Gate itu menerapkan `reference_rotation` sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pooling the samples from all five Krylov circuits, the support is tiny: a few hundred distinct bitstrings out of the $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ determinants in the `(4, 4)` sector. This concentration, a direct consequence of the momentum-basis sparsity established in step 2, makes the subsequent classical diagonalization tractable.\n"
msgstr "Dengan menggabungkan sampel dari kelima circuit Krylov, dukungannya sangat kecil: beberapa ratus bitstring berbeda dari $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ determinan di sektor `(4, 4)`. Konsentrasi ini, konsekuensi langsung dari sparsity basis momentum yang ditetapkan di langkah 2, membuat diagonalisasi klasik berikutnya tertangani.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plotting the counts with [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) makes the sparsity visible. A few configurations dominate, led by the reference determinant.\n"
msgstr "Memplot hasil hitungan dengan [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) membuat sparsitasnya terlihat jelas. Beberapa konfigurasi mendominasi, dipimpin oleh determinan referensi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Histogram of the bitstrings sampled from the Krylov circuits, showing a small support.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-16.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Histogram of the bitstrings sampled from the Krylov circuits, showing a small support.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-16.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Diagonalize in the sampled subspace {#7-diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace}"
msgstr "7. Diagonalisasi dalam subruang hasil sampling {#7-diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sampled bitstrings are the input to the classical half of SKQD. The Hamiltonian is projected onto the subspace the sampled configurations span and diagonalized there. This is passed to the [qiskit-addon-sqd](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd) package, whose [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"(in Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD))\") runs the full sample-based quantum diagonalization loop. It builds a subspace from batches of the sampled configurations, diagonalizes the Hamiltonian in it, and iteratively refines the subspace by using configuration recovery: flipping occupations to repair configurations that violate the known particle-number symmetry. Configuration recovery is designed to undo the damage of hardware noise, which corrupts sampled bitstrings into the wrong particle-number sector; the sampling here is noiseless, so there is nothing to repair on that front.\n"
msgstr "Bitstring hasil sampling menjadi input untuk bagian klasik dari SKQD. Hamiltonian diproyeksikan ke subruang yang direntang oleh konfigurasi hasil sampling, lalu didiagonalisasi di sana. Ini diteruskan ke paket [qiskit-addon-sqd](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), yang fungsi [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"(in Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD))\")-nya menjalankan seluruh loop sample-based quantum diagonalization. Fungsi ini membangun subruang dari batch konfigurasi hasil sampling, mendiagonalisasi Hamiltonian di dalamnya, dan menyempurnakan subruang secara iteratif dengan configuration recovery: membalik okupansi untuk memperbaiki konfigurasi yang melanggar simetri jumlah partikel yang diketahui. Configuration recovery dirancang untuk membalikkan kerusakan akibat noise hardware, yang merusak bitstring hasil sampling sehingga masuk ke sektor jumlah partikel yang salah; sampling di sini bebas noise, jadi tidak ada yang perlu diperbaiki dari sisi itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The solver consumes the sampled counts as a [`BitArray`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray), built directly from the pooled `counts` of step 6. Pass `num_bits` explicitly: without it, the width is inferred from the widest sampled bitstring, which is narrower than `2 * norb` whenever no sample occupies the last mode, and the solver then rejects the array. The solver diagonalizes in the same momentum basis the rest of the construction uses, so it takes the `h1e_momentum` and `h2e_momentum` integrals from step 2 directly, with no repacking. The recovered energy matches the exact reference to well under a milli-Hartree, from only a few hundred sampled configurations. Because the SQD energy is a variational upper bound on the true ground state, it always sits at or above `reference_energy` (still in scope from step 2):\n"
msgstr "Solver memakai hasil hitungan sampling sebagai [`BitArray`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray), yang dibangun langsung dari `counts` gabungan di langkah 6. Berikan `num_bits` secara eksplisit: tanpa itu, lebarnya disimpulkan dari bitstring hasil sampling terlebar, yang lebih sempit dari `2 * norb` kapan pun tidak ada sampel yang menempati mode terakhir, dan solver lalu menolak array tersebut. Solver mendiagonalisasi dalam basis momentum yang sama dengan yang dipakai di seluruh konstruksi lainnya, jadi solver langsung memakai integral `h1e_momentum` dan `h2e_momentum` dari langkah 2, tanpa pengemasan ulang. Energi hasil pemulihan cocok dengan referensi eksak hingga jauh di bawah satu milli-Hartree, dari hanya beberapa ratus konfigurasi hasil sampling. Karena energi SQD adalah batas atas variasional untuk ground state sebenarnya, nilainya selalu sama dengan atau di atas `reference_energy` (yang masih tersedia dari langkah 2):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the run: the energy’s convergence across the iterations, and the average occupancy of each spatial orbital in the recovered ground state. The per-iteration energy is the lowest across that iteration’s batches, and the occupancy sums the `orbital_occupancies` over the two spin sectors. Even without noise to correct, the energy decreases from iteration to iteration. Each iteration diagonalizes within `num_batches` batches of only `samples_per_batch` configurations subsampled from the pool, and the iterative refinement due to bitstring carryover steadily improves which configurations land in those batches, so the recovered energy improves:\n"
msgstr "Visualisasikan hasil run: konvergensi energi di sepanjang iterasi, dan okupansi rata-rata tiap orbital spasial pada ground state hasil pemulihan. Energi per iterasi adalah yang terendah dari semua batch pada iterasi tersebut, dan okupansi menjumlahkan `orbital_occupancies` atas kedua sektor spin. Bahkan tanpa noise yang perlu dikoreksi, energi menurun dari iterasi ke iterasi. Setiap iterasi mendiagonalisasi dalam `num_batches` batch yang masing-masing hanya berisi `samples_per_batch` konfigurasi yang disubsampel dari kumpulan, dan penyempurnaan iteratif berkat bitstring carryover terus memperbaiki konfigurasi mana yang masuk ke batch tersebut, sehingga energi hasil pemulihan membaik:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![SQD energy convergence and the average occupancy per spatial orbital.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-18.avif)\n"
msgstr "![SQD energy convergence and the average occupancy per spatial orbital.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-18.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This closes the SKQD loop. The momentum-basis circuits of steps 1–5 produce a sparse sample (step 6), and the sample-based diagonalization above turns that sample back into a ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr "Ini menutup loop SKQD. Circuit basis momentum dari langkah 1–5 menghasilkan sampel yang sparse (langkah 6), dan diagonalisasi berbasis sampel di atas mengubah sampel itu kembali menjadi energi ground state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah berikutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide ran the whole SKQD pipeline on a noiseless statevector simulator. On hardware, the transpiled `circuits` would be executed and measured in place of the statevector sampling in step 6, with the resulting counts feeding the step-7 diagonalization unchanged. Refer to the [Qiskit documentation](/guides/intro-to-patterns) for help running circuits, and to the [SQD addon tutorials](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/overview) for information about the subspace-diagonalization post-processing, including its behavior on noisy samples, where configuration recovery does the most work.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menjalankan seluruh pipeline SKQD pada simulator statevector tanpa noise. Pada hardware, `circuits` yang sudah ditranspilasi akan dieksekusi dan diukur sebagai pengganti sampling statevector di langkah 6, dengan hasil hitungan yang diperoleh masuk ke diagonalisasi langkah 7 tanpa perubahan. Lihat [dokumentasi Qiskit](/guides/intro-to-patterns) untuk bantuan menjalankan circuit, dan [tutorial addon SQD](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/overview) untuk informasi tentang post-processing diagonalisasi subruang, termasuk perilakunya pada sampel yang noisy, di mana configuration recovery bekerja paling banyak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the [ffsim relationship guide](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation) to understand why [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") and [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") work natively on this package’s fermionic circuits, and why the fixed-particle-number sector used in step 6 makes the momentum-basis sparsity established in step 2 sample-efficient.\n"
msgstr "Baca [panduan hubungan ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation) untuk memahami mengapa [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") dan [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") bekerja secara native pada circuit fermionik paket ini, dan mengapa sektor jumlah partikel tetap yang dipakai di langkah 6 membuat sparsitas basis momentum yang ditetapkan di langkah 2 efisien dalam sampling.\n"
